# Working on this repo

Read `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/DECISIONS.md` before starting. They are the source of truth; this file only covers your workflow.

## When Nathan says "do issue #N"

1. Read the issue: `gh issue view N`. The issue is your whole brief. Its acceptance criteria are what "done" means. If something is unclear or contradicts `CLAUDE.md`, ask Nathan instead of guessing.
2. Start from the latest main: `git switch main && git pull`, then `git switch -c feat/N-short-name` (or `fix/N-short-name`).
3. Do what the issue asks, and only that. Keep the diff small. Follow the layered layout: imports only go downward (controllers → services → repositories/clients → models).
4. Add tests for any new logic. No test may call the real Claude API unless it is marked `@pytest.mark.live`.
5. Run every check that exists in the repo and fix failures before you commit:
   - `ruff check .`
   - `ruff format --check .`
   - `lint-imports`
   - `pytest`
   - `luacheck game/` and `busted tests/lua`
6. Commit with a clear message, then `git push -u origin <branch>`.
7. Open the PR: `gh pr create --base main --title "<issue title>" --body "..."`. Write the body in the format under "PR descriptions" below.
8. Tell Nathan the PR number and stop. Claude Code reviews it.

## PR descriptions

Nathan reads every PR and is new to modding and git. Write for him, not for a reviewer. Plain English, short sentences, no wall of file names or code. Use this shape and keep the whole body under about 25 lines:

```
Closes #N

**What this does:** one or two sentences a non-programmer understands. Say what now works, not how.

**What changed**
- 3–5 short bullets, one per piece (e.g. "Python can now write an order for the game")

**Checks:** ruff ✅ · format ✅ · lint-imports ✅ · pytest ✅ (19 passed) · busted ✅/not run (say why in one line)

**How to test in game** (only if the issue has an in-game checklist)
1. Short numbered steps, copied from the issue
```

- Put each check on one line with its result. Don't paste raw tool output unless a check failed.
- Leave out implementation details (function names, retry counts, parsing rules). The diff and the reviewer cover those.
- If something didn't work or was skipped, say so plainly in one line.

## When the review says Changes requested

Read the review with `gh pr view N --comments`. Fix each point on the same branch, re-run the checks, commit, and push. Then reply on the PR with what you changed.

## Never

- Push to `main`, merge a PR, or force-push.
- Commit `.env`, API keys, game files, or `.pack` files.
- Work on more than one issue per branch.
